        "d7624e53-96f3-43a2-a5b4-052847d8844f": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": true,
            "title": "Setting Up",
            "text": "<p>1) Remove all the contents from inside of the vacuum cleaner container.<br/><br/>2) Turn the container upside down and insert the feet with casters into the slots and apply pressure until they click into place. Secure them with supplied screws.<br/><br/>3) Your vacuum cleaner comes ready for dry vacuum cleaning with the washable cartridge filter and pre-filter pre-installed.<br/><br/>4) For wet vacuum cleaning, remove the pre-filter.<br/><br/>5) Secure the power head back on the container using the latches. Make sure the power head is properly installed with the blowing port positioned in the back of the unit.<br/><br/>6) Insert the locking end of the suction hose into the suction port of the container.<br/><br/>7) Choose the desired accessories and/or extension wands and push fit onto the suction hose nozzle.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "black",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "link",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
            "product_specifications": "",
            "html": "",
            "collection": "",
            "collection_products_per_page": 8,
            "products": [],
            "image_loading": "",
            "video_1": "",
            "video_2": ""
          }
        },
        "80d3ee7d-e860-4a9c-8b84-2c5508cdf136": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": true,
            "title": "Operating & Maintaining",
            "text": "<p><strong>Switching On/Off</strong><br/>Connect the mains plug to a suitable power outlet. Position Status:<br/>I On<br/>O Off<br/><br/><strong>Wet & Dry Vacuum Operation</strong><br/><br/>1) Verify that the correct filter is installed for wet or dry vacuuming and the tank latches are secured.<br/><br/>2) Secure the locking end of the suction hose into the vacuum suction port.<br/><br/>3) Push the desired accessories onto the hose nozzle. The air flow regulation allows you to change vacuum cleaner suction. <br/><br/>4) Plug the power cord into a power outlet.<br/><br/>5) Turn on the appliance by assigning the switch to the “I” ON position.<br/><br/>6) Once you have completed vacuuming, switch to the “O” OFF position and unplug the power cord from the power outlet.<br/><br/>NOTE: If vacuuming a mixture of wet and dry surfaces, fully clean and dry the filters and container after each use.<br/><br/><strong>For Dry Vacuuming:</strong><br/><br/>1) To prepare your vacuum cleaner for dry vacuuming, install the cartridge filter over the filter cage with the flat end of the filter towards the vacuum power head. Carefully push the filter until it sits flush forming a tight seal.<br/><br/>2 )Place the filter retainer on top of the cartridge filter over the raised lip and tighten the retainer lock clockwise to secure against the internal filter cage.<br/><br/>3) Place the nylon pre-filter over the cartridge filter, making sure the whole filter is covered and securing the drawstring. Replace the power head, and secure it in place.<br/><br/><strong>For Wet Vacuuming:</strong><br/><br/>1) To prepare your vacuum cleaner for wet vacuuming, remove the pre-filter. Verify that the washable cartridge filter is installed.<br/><br/>NOTE: Please make sure the washable cartridge filter is dry before using it for wet vacuuming.</p><p>The vacuum cleaner is equipped with a float valve which is operational during wet suction. The suction power decreases when the maximum filling level is reached. You will notice an increase in motor noise. When this happens, switch the vacuum cleaner off immediately, and empty the container.<br/><br/><strong>Blower Operation</strong><br/><br/>1) Make sure the container and any collected waste is emptied and the filter is dry before using as a blower.<br/><br/>2) Insert the locking end of the suction hose into the blowing port on the rear of the power head.<br/><br/>3) Turn on the motor by turning the switch to the ‘I’ ON position.<br/><br/><strong>For Detachable Blowing Operation</strong><br/><br/>1) Hold the blower handle and press the blower release button to lift the detachable blower fromthe blower housing.<br/><br/>2) Secure the locking end of the blower adapter onto the blower port (Fig. 13).<br/><br/>3) Fit the blower tube onto the adapter. Make sure the blower tube is secured into place (Fig. 14).<br/> <br/>4) Firmly hold the blower before turning it on. Turn the appliance on by turning the switch to the ‘I’<br/>ON position.<br/><br/>NOTE: Make sure that the detachable blower is replaced properly onto the blower housing when<br/>finished blowing.<br/><br/><strong>Cleaning Washable Cartridge Filter & Nylon Pre-filter</strong><br/><br/>1) Remove the filter and clean by gently tapping or brushing dirt off. For optimal performance it is recommended to replace the old filter with a new filter regularly.<br/><br/>2) Use a mild soap and water solution to wash cartridge filter and nylon pre-filter and rinse with clean water. Allow the filters to air dry completely before storing or re-installing.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
